  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A solid box is \\(15\\) cm by \\(10\\) cm by \\(8\\) cm. A new solid is formed by removing a cube \\(3\\) cm on a side from each corner of this box. What percent of the original volume is removed?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(4.5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(9\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(18\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(24\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "18"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2003-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The original volume is \\(15 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 8 = 1200.\\)\n\nEight corner cubes are removed, each of volume \\(3^3 = 27,\\) totaling \\(8 \\cdot 27 = 216.\\)\n\nThe fraction removed is \\(\\dfrac{216}{1200} = 0.18,\\) which is \\(18\\%.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "The box has \\(8\\) corners",
        "Each removed cube has volume \\(3^3\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
